   "text": "In a randomized, double-blind trial of 1,284 adults (mean age 61.3 years), daily supplementation with 2,000 IU of vitamin D3 did not reduce the incidence of type 2 diabetes compared with placebo (hazard ratio, 0.88; 95% CI, 0.75 to 1.04; p = 0.12). Serum 25-hydroxyvitamin D rose from 28 to 54 ng/mL. These findings are consistent with earlier meta-analyses [12, 14] but contrast with observational data reported by Pittas et al.",
   "normalized": "In a randomized, double-blind trial of one thousand, two hundred eighty-four adults, mean age sixty-one point three years, daily supplementation with two thousand I U of vitamin D three did not reduce the incidence of type two diabetes compared with placebo, hazard ratio, zero point eight eight; ninety-five percent confidence interval, zero point seven five to one point zero four; p equals zero point one two. Serum twenty-five-hydroxyvitamin D rose from twenty-eight to fifty-four nanograms per milliliter. These findings are consistent with earlier meta-analyses but contrast with observational data reported by Pittas and colleagues.",
